1. THE REQUIREMENT AND ITS THREE CHECKS
   REQ-016 (v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml), verbatim: "The solar input charges the pack through board E's LT8705A stage from a panel inside its declared window: an open-circuit voltage of at most 25 V at the panel's coldest operating temperature, the panel held at 17.6 V by the stage's input regulation, and at most 100 W into the stage."
   read: at most 25 V open circuit at the panel's coldest operating temperature; held at 17.6 V; at most 100 W into the stage;
   its acceptance: F2 and J_SOLAR rated 10 A; and "Protection is judged apart from the window, under rule TRN-001". A series diode or a clamp in place of the panel's own open
   circuit: NOT admitted (the statement constrains the panel's own open circuit)
   THE WINDOW (normal operation, REQ-016's rated quantity): the makers' rated Voc row is defined at 1000 W/m2 (SunPower 523809
   p.1: 'Typical Electrical Data at STC: 25°C, 1000 W/m² and AM 1.5'; Solbian's STC note and BougeRV's rows alike), moved to the coldest operating
   temperature, -20 C, REQ-024's in-use minimum (-20 to +40 C ambient; pcb_envelope.yaml in_use agrees). The records settle
   REQ-016's reading there (L4-ENERGY-ARCHITECTURE.md, 'What stays INCONCLUSIVE'); the panels' -40 C ratings are information.
   No irradiance above 1000 W/m2 enters the window: the earlier G_MAX of 2111.4 W/m2 is WITHDRAWN as a decision input.
   THE DISTURBANCE CHECK (component limits during an irradiance burst on cold-soaked cells, seconds to minutes): judged apart
   from the window under TRN-001, against the lowest rating on PV_P (section 11); it needs no irradiance maximum.
   USEFUL POWER (A-2): the stage draws its own drive and quiescent power, 42.3 mA, 1.27 W at L4-E5's raised EXTVCC (L4-E7,
   INFERRED there), from its output; at its declared 0.93 (the replay) the input must exceed 1.27 / 0.93 = 1.365591 W.
   CONTEXT, not a bound: E0 = 1361 W/m2 / (1 - 0.0167)^2 = 1407.6 W/m2, the extraterrestrial irradiance at perihelion (physical
   constants); the read source (Mol and van Heerwaarden 2025, ACP 25, p.1, CC BY 4.0): "In cloud fields with enough optically thin area, such as altocumulus, forward escape alone can drive areas of irradiance enhancement of over 50 % of clear-sky irradiance."
   and the clear-sky noon irradiance at Cabauw near 1000 W/m2 (Mol, Knap and van Heerwaarden 2023, p.8). The kit's in-use
   altitude reaches 3000 m (D-02c).
   owner rulings in the registry naming a panel class (a class word beside 'panel' or 'array' in one sentence): none; a1solar SELECTION.md 1 (a session's criterion) prefers folding, semi-rigid or blanket for a carried kit

