11. THE DISTURBANCE CHECK: COMPONENT LIMITS DURING AN IRRADIANCE BURST ON COLD-SOAKED CELLS (TRN-001, apart from the window)
   THE LIMIT: the lowest rating on PV_P for a current-limited source held for minutes is D4's printed standoff, the SMCJ28A's
   VR 28.0 V (at most 1 uA there; Littelfuse SMCJ sheet p.2, the row VR 28.0 / VBR 31.10 to 34.40 V at 1 mA / VC 45.4 V at 33.1 A /
   IR 1 uA). The sheet prints VBR(TJ) = VBR(25 C) x (1 + aT (TJ - 25)), aT typical 0.1 %/C (p.1): the cold VBR minimum at -20 C
   is 29.70 V (a typical coefficient). C11 and C12's 35 V lie above.
   THE IRRADIANCE TERM, by junction physics, not by a measured slope: dVoc / d ln G <= n x Ns x kT/q, Ns 32 (the sheet), T 253.15 K
   (kT/q 0.021815 V); n_max = 2 is a MODELLING_ASSUMPTION (the silicon junction's ideality ceiling: 1 for diffusion, 2 for
   depletion-region recombination); M3's measured n = A25 / (Ns kT/q at 298.15 K, 0.025693 V) must read at or under 2 with its
   uncertainty, else this check is re-judged (the typical unit's fit: n 1.2981, 1.4279 with U_A).
   THE COLDEST CELLS ARE THE WORST CASE: d/dT [Voc(T, 1000) + n Ns kT/q ln(G / 1000)] = beta + n Ns k/q ln(G / 1000); up to the
   threshold below the second term is at most 3.000 V / 253.15 K = 0.011851 V/K, against the sheet's coefficient of at least 0.0589 V/K
   in magnitude (the smaller of its two readings): the derivative stays negative, so cells warmer than -20 C give less.
   THE THRESHOLD: a unit at A-1's ceiling (Vm20 + U_V = 25.000 V) reaches D4's 28.0 V standoff at G = 1000 exp(3.000 V / (n Ns kT/q)):
     n from the typical unit's fit (INFERRED)                 n 1.2981: 0.9062 V per unit of ln G; 27401 W/m2, 19.47 x E0
     n_max = 2 (MODELLING_ASSUMPTION): the decision row       n 2.0000: 1.3961 V per unit of ln G; 8574 W/m2, 6.09 x E0
     n = 3 (a sensitivity)                                    n 3.0000: 2.0942 V per unit of ln G; 4189 W/m2, 2.98 x E0
   RESULT: the disturbance check is implied by A-1 for every plane-of-array irradiance below 8574 W/m2 (n <= 2), 6.09 x the
   extraterrestrial irradiance; no irradiance maximum is a decision input. ASSUMPTION: the plane-of-array irradiance stays below
   that threshold (the context of section 1 puts the read enhancement at 2111.4 W/m2 on E0). Its impact if it fails: D4 rises above
   its standoff and conducts under 1 mA until its VBR (29.70 V cold minimum), no damage below VBR. Its verification: none beyond
   M3's n check (M5 optional). Cross-check: SunPower's own allowance, 1.25 x Voc for component voltage ratings, is 26.75 V on the
   rated row and 27.69 V at the window's Voc25 ceiling, both under the 28.0 V standoff.

12. THE DECISION ON U-03 (SESSION): TWO ROUTES
   Route 1, a maker-bound sheet: bounded in the window by the printed band AND the hold inside the curve at the conditioned upper
   corner over that band AND portable:
     SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100                                      bounded NO; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
     BougeRV 100W N-Type Fiberglass Foldable (SP001-BK-GRUSGA)    bounded yes; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
     Solbian SX 156                                               bounded NO; hold yes; portable yes -> does not qualify
     on EA3's typical band (upper corner 18.221 V) instead: SPR does not qualify; BGV does not qualify; SBX does not qualify
   Route 2, a controlled unit: PANEL-ACC's contract (section 10) has a non-empty window that holds the identified panel's typical
   rows, with A-1, A-2, A-3(a) and A-3(b) met at the specification: yes
   U-03: CONDITIONAL DOWNSTREAM UNIT SELECTION (PANEL-ACC).
   It is not an architecture-level choice: REQ-016's window, the stage, its hold and its 100 W control stay, and the panel is
   selected downstream by measurement. It is CONDITIONAL on: a bought unit passing A-1, A-2 and A-3(b) by its own measurement
   (M1 to M3 and A-2's reading at the specification); L4-E7R's regulation and backstop applied (A-3(a) and A-4, the backstop's
   93.5521 W CONDITIONAL on G_CM and the VIN+ bias); A-3(c)'s connector and conductor rating at Layer 5/6; the disturbance check's
   assumption (section 11) and M3's n;
   the unit's trace rerun (A1, A2). None of these can overturn the architecture: A-3(c) is a connector rating (REQ-016's 'rated
   10 A' is a minimum), and the rest decide a unit, not the topology.
   NO PHYSICAL UNIT IS ACCEPTED: none is bought or measured; the purchase and the measurement are the owner's actions (money).
   Route 1 stays open beside it: the drafts in clarification/ ask the two hold-matched makers for a warranted band (the owner
   sends them; the session contacts no outside party). REQ-016 need not change, so no owner question is raised.
   THE DOWNSTREAM ITEM, PANEL-ACC (Layer 6, component selection; the purchase is the owner's): accept the panel by route 1 (the
   bought revision's document, filed with its sha256, bounds its band in the window and keeps the hold inside the curve, sections
   3 and 4) or by route 2 (the identified unit passes A-1, A-2 and A-3(b) at the specification, section 10); in either case rerun
   its trace through the replay's section 12 and L4-E7's section 5 (A1 and A2), rate J_SOLAR and PV_IN for A-3(c), keep F2's and
   J_SOLAR's 10 A minimum and the 100 W on L4-E7's limit (A-3(a), A-4), and check M3's n against the disturbance threshold.

13. EVIDENCE CLASSES: MAKER (SunPower's sheet and guide, Solbian's sheet, Littelfuse's SMCJ sheet, JST's VH catalogue),
    MAKER-PAGE (BougeRV's page, transcribed), RECORD (the replay's and L4-E7's outputs, the stage's drive power), LITERATURE
    (the enhancement and the Cabauw quotations, CC BY 4.0, context only), MODELED (the energy record's single-diode model and day),
    INFERRED (the window ratios, the demonstration unit, A-2's signs, the cell temperature at the hot end), ASSUMPTION (S0 and the
    orbit's eccentricity as physical constants; a band's voltages scaled with its currents kept; BougeRV's rows taken as STC; the
    irradiance below the disturbance threshold), MODELLING_ASSUMPTION (n_max = 2), COMPONENT_LIMITATION (J_SOLAR prints no
    short-time overload), SESSION (the window's reading, the 10 % sentence's reading, the hold screen, the conditioned band,
    PANEL-ACC's unit, measurements and specification, the useful-power line, A-3(c)'s design level).
